      "description": "Timer, soft 3-minute guide, and straw progress track with the guide tick.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-clock\"><div class=\"ds-clock-row\"><span class=\"ds-time\">1:12</span><span class=\"ds-guide\">about 3 min</span></div><div class=\"ds-track\"><i style=\"width:24%\"></i><b style=\"left:60%\"></b></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-clock{font-family:'Hanken Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;width:340px;color:var(--ink,#eef0f3);font-size:15px;} .ds-clock-row{display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;} .ds-time{font-size:24px;font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;letter-spacing:-0.01em;} .ds-guide{color:var(--ink-soft,#a3aab6);} .ds-track{position:relative;height:4px;margin-top:10px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--rule,#2a2f3a);} .ds-track i{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:2px;background:var(--gel-straw,#d8c98f);} .ds-track b{position:absolute;top:-4px;width:2px;height:12px;border-radius:1px;background:var(--ink-faint,#7c8391);}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lighting Rig",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": null,
      "description": "Signature stage: straw spike tape (centre cross + two T-marks on the floor line) while unlit; open-white beam and floor pool driven by voice level; resolves into labelled translucent gels after saving.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-rig\"><svg class=\"ds-mark\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"><path d=\"M47.5 68h5M50 65.5v5\" vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"/><path d=\"M15 68h5M17.5 68v3\" vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"/><path d=\"M80 68h5M82.5 68v3\" vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"/></svg></div><div class=\"ds-rig\"><div class=\"ds-beam\"></div><div class=\"ds-pool\"></div></div><div class=\"ds-rig\"><div class=\"ds-gel\" style=\"--g:var(--gel-sea,#57b39a);left:44%;top:46%;width:66%;height:66%;opacity:.74\"></div><div class=\"ds-gel\" style=\"--g:var(--gel-straw,#d8c98f);left:64%;top:38%;width:50%;height:50%;opacity:.6\"></div><div class=\"ds-gel\" style=\"--g:var(--gel-violet,#8f72de);left:58%;top:64%;width:40%;height:40%;opacity:.5\"></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-rig{position:relative;display:inline-block;width:200px;height:200px;margin:4px;background:var(--stage,#0f1116);overflow:hidden;isolation:isolate;} .ds-mark{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:visible;fill:none;stroke:var(--gel-straw,#d8c98f);stroke-opacity:.5;stroke-width:2;stroke-linecap:round;transition:opacity 600ms cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);} .ds-beam{position:absolute;left:50%;top:-8%;width:84%;height:76%;transform:translateX(-50%);clip-path:polygon(42% 0,58% 0,100% 100%,0 100%);background:linear-gradient(to bottom,rgb(255 238 200/0),rgb(255 238 200/.16) 70%,rgb(255 238 200/.05));opacity:.7;mix-blend-mode:screen;} .ds-pool{position:absolute;left:50%;top:68%;width:84%;height:34%;border-radius:50%;mix-blend-mode:screen;background:radial-gradient(closest-side,rgb(255 244 218) 0,rgb(246 226 180/.82) 34%,rgb(216 201 143/.34) 68%,rgb(216 201 143/0) 100%);opacity:.7;transform:translate(-50%,-50%) scale(.9);} .ds-gel{position:absolute;border-radius:50%;mix-blend-mode:screen;background:radial-gradient(closest-side,var(--g) 0 88%,transparent 100%);transform:translate(-50%,-50%);}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Lighting Gels",
    "overview": "A theatre lighting gel swatch book laid out on a dark stage. The screen is a blue-black theatre used in a dark bedroom at night; the only light on it is the user's own voice. While recording, a single open-white lamp throws a beam down onto the floor and its pool brightens and spreads with the voice. When the entry is saved, the light resolves into overlapping translucent gels, one per emotion, whose size and density carry confidence, each paired with a labelled swatch tag below the stage.\n\nThe system is quiet and low-energy by design: two type sizes ranked by weight, panels only one step lighter than the ground, large rounded thumb-reach buttons where the light button is always the primary action. Colour is reserved for meaning. The six named gels plus Open white are the only chromatic values on screen, and a gel never appears without its name.\n\nDepth comes from light, not from shadow. Beam, pool and gels are additive (screen-blended) light on black; surfaces are flat tonal steps.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark stage ground (stage) with flat panels one step up; no shadows anywhere.",
      "A fixed gel set mapped one-to-one to emotions, always labelled with name + soft word.",
      "Voice level is the only live driver of the stage; everything else is still.",
      "Hanken Grotesk at two working sizes (15px and 24px), hierarchy by weight.",
      "56px rounded buttons in the bottom thumb zone; light = primary, dark = secondary."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Labelled Gel Rule",
        "body": "A gel colour never appears without its swatch tag naming the emotion and a soft confidence word. Colour is never the only carrier of meaning.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Gels Mean Feelings Rule",
        "body": "The six gel colours are reserved for emotions (Straw also carries the interface accent). Don't use a gel as decoration, a brand colour, or a category colour for anything else.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Lamp Rule",
        "body": "While recording, the stage holds one open-white lamp only. Gel colour appears on the stage only after the entry has been read.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Sizes Rule",
        "body": "The working sizes are 15px and 24px. Rank by weight and ink tone, not by adding sizes.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Soft Words Rule",
        "body": "Confidence is spoken, never numbered. Swatch tags use \"strong\", \"clear\", \"a little\", \"faint\"; the reading sentence uses \"mostly\", \"a little\", \"some\", \"a trace of\". No percentages, scores or bars for emotion.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Light Not Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Depth is light added to the stage, never shadow cast beneath a surface.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Voice Drives Light Rule",
        "body": "Beam opacity and pool size/brightness follow the live voice level and nothing else. Unlit (idle, which includes failed and denied) shows only the spike tape on the floor; paused dims the pool to 0.12; listening-back breathes the pool slowly (2.8s, 0.18–0.42 opacity).",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** pair every gel colour on screen with a swatch tag naming the emotion and a soft confidence word.",
      "**Do** keep the primary action as the light button (ink fill) in the bottom row, 56px tall.",
      "**Do** let the voice level be the only live driver of stage light; everything else on screen stays still while recording.",
      "**Do** draw gels at the fixed rig scale and slot positions every night so nights compare by eye.",
